+
+## PR integration and CI repair
+
+Before opening a PR, Autocatalyst integrates the target branch and reviews the combined
+tree. If Activity reports a conflict, an authorized host operator uses the repository,
+run ID and source branch shown there to locate the retained workspace under its configured
+root. Confirm the branch and recorded commit before making changes. Commit the resolution
+and leave a clean worktree, then use Resume. If only the branch remains, use the normal
+run-branch materialization. If the branch expired, Resume cannot recover it.
+
+Periodic CI watching is off by default. To enable it, set
+`AUTOCATALYST_PR_RECONCILE_TICKER=true`, a positive `AUTOCATALYST_PR_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS`
+and one `AUTOCATALYST_PR_RECONCILE_TENANT`. Authorize the reconciliation system principal
+for that tenant. Other tenants, and deployments with the ticker off, can observe CI
+through authorized batch reconciliation. Otherwise follow the PR link to check CI on GitHub.
+
+`AUTOCATALYST_PR_CI_REPAIR_LIMIT` defaults to 2 admitted attempts per PR. Set it to a
+nonnegative safe integer; 0 disables new repair attempts without disabling CI observation
+or terminal reconciliation. Repairs update the same PR and never merge it.
+
+If Activity says a workspace is held after an interruption, do not dispatch, materialize or
+clean it up. An authorized host operator confirms old workers and pushes are finished before
+salvaging it. Engineers can continue from an authorized clone and merge or close on GitHub.
+There is no product action to release an unconfirmed hold.
